<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Ortiz jets off to Europe for Davos summit.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Ortiz jets off to Europe for Davos summit.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Finance Minister Guillermo Ortiz jetted off Wednesday for Europe to promote economic and financial relations with France, Switzerland and Germany, the Finance Ministry said.</p>
<p>In Switzerland, Ortiz will attend various events around the annual Davos economic summit.  First, Ortiz will travel to Paris to meet his French counterpart Jean Arthuis and also Bank of France Governor Jean Claude Trichet.</p>
<p>Following Davos, Ortiz will travel on to Frankfurt, where he will meet Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer and later will have private meetings with bankers, the ministry said.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom =525 7289530))</p>
